      "writtenOn": "2022-06-14T23:15:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does it make sense to set avrcp volume but not hfp volume if address is invalid. I feel like you should set both or neither.\n\ni.e.\n\n```\nlet addr \u003d match RawAddress::from_string(device.clone()) {\n  Some(v) \u003d\u003e v,\n  None \u003d\u003e {\n    warn!(\"Invalid device string {}\", device);\n    return;\n  }\n};\n\n\nif let Ok(val) \u003d i8::try_from(volume) {\n  self.hfp.as_mut().unwrap().set_volume(val, addr);\n  self.avrcp.as_mut().unwrap().set_volume(val);\n}\n```",
      "revId": "a9debe126f43e0d56ebae58776f4829ddf0eb4cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89006b8d_28a4bc72",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
